            <div xml:id="d103">

                <pb facs="0338" n="301" sameAs="frus:frus1951-54Iran/pg301"/>

                <head>103. Telegram From the Department of State to the Embassy in Iran<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d103-f1"/></head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1952-07-29T20:00:00-04:00">July 29, 1952, 8 p.m</date>.</dateline>
                <p>255. Brit
                    Emb reps called this morning to discuss
                    complicated and ominous Iran situation. We here do not see the possibility at
                    this time of a more constructive alternative to Mosadeq for the reasons outlined in our 585 July 26.<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d103-f2"/> However, in view of Mosadeq’s attitude as expressed in your 423 July 28 we believe
                    that every possibility should be reexplored.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d103-f3"/> It
                    was therefore agreed request US-Brit
                    Emb in Tehran make joint reappraisal situation
                    to include (A) recommendations as to possible joint courses action by US–UK; (B) possible
                    alternatives to Mosadeq (C) methods bring
                    such alternative to power; (D) form encouragement and support which would be
                    necessary.</p>
                <p>FYI Brits expressed grave concern re
                    developments Iran and stated primary objective now is to save Iran from
                    communism. However, at same time impression gained that Brits not yet willing
                    capitulate entirely to Irans in oil dispute even though this position might mean
                    loss Iran to West.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed corresp="#p_ADG_1">Acheson</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
